{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-18354-r4617976","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Baklava I","sourcePageId":18354,"sourceRevision":"4617976","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-06T20:58:57Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Baklava%20I&oldid=4617976","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:56.684Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Greek recipes","Category:Halal recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes for pastries","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using phyllo","Category:Recipes using walnut","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Turkish recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"2b31fe1ac21d99d1f01cc255d5020b58f49abc53018f5f6dcae2d36eb6bca73a","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Recipes for dessert\n| Difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[File:Baklava(RobertK).jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Desserts]]\n__NOTOC__\n==Ingredients==\n{{metricate}}\n\n=== Pastry ===\n*1 [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]] (454 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[cookbook:Phyllo dough|phyllo dough]]\n*4–5 [[cookbook:cup|cup]] [[cookbook:walnuts|walnuts]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] coarsely\n*½ cup white granulated [[cookbook:sugar|sugar]]\n*¼ [[cookbook:tsp|tsp]] [[wikt:ground|ground]] [[cookbook:clove|cloves]]\n*1 tsp [[cookbook:cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n*¾ pound (340 g) sweet [[cookbook:butter|butter]]\n\n=== Syrup ===\n*2 ½ cups of [[cookbook:water|water]]\n*3 cups white granulated [[cookbook:sugar|sugar]]\n*3 tsp [[cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n*1 tsp [[cookbook:vanilla Extract|vanilla extract]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Pastry ===\n#Combine nuts, cinnamon, cloves, and sugar. Melt butter in a [[cookbook:saucepan|saucepan]].\n#Use a pastry [[Cookbook:Brush|brush]] to brush inside of a 14 x 10.5-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] (36 x 27 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]]) pan with melted butter. \n#Line bottom of pan with one piece of Phyllo dough. Fold under excess Phyllo.\n#Alternate sides with each piece of Phyllo, brushing the top of each layer with melted butter.\n#Repeat 5 times, making 5 layers.\n#On the 6th sheet, sprinkle evenly with nut mixture.\n#Continue until all nut mixture is used and last 6 buttered sheets of Phyllo form top crust.\n#Use a sharp knife to cut into diamond shapes.\n#[[cookbook:Bake|Bake]] at 300 °F (150 °C) for about 1 ½ hours or until lightly brown.\n\n=== Syrup ===\n#Combine syrup ingredients. [[cookbook:Boil|Boil]] syrup for about 10 minutes and then allow to cool. \n#Pour cooled syrup over hot pastry. Enjoy!\n\n[[Category:Greek recipes|Baklava]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert|Baklava]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pastries|Baklava]]\n[[Category:Recipes using walnut]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Halal recipes|Baklava]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes with images]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using phyllo]]\n[[Category:Turkish recipes]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Baklava I","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[],"steps":[],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:18354","recordId":"wikibooks-18354-r4617976","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4617976","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Baklava%20I&oldid=4617976","sourceSha256":"2b31fe1ac21d99d1f01cc255d5020b58f49abc53018f5f6dcae2d36eb6bca73a","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"source-prefix-v2","license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"reviewStatus":"source-extracted-unreviewed","changeNotice":"Source-language section extraction; markup removed. Not culinarily reviewed, translated or runtime-approved.","recipe":{"name":"Baklava I","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText